<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Far Eastern Jan-Sept profit down.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Far Eastern Jan-Sept profit down.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-September 1996</p>
<p>		(in million Taiwan $ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Turnover				21,602 vs 25,242</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			    752 vs  3,022</p>
<p>Note - Far Eastern Textile Ltd is Taiwan's largest textile maker. The company has attributed the profit plunge to the sluggish sales and prices in the polyester fibre industry and smaller non-operating profits in the first three quarters of 1996 than a year earlier. The firm has set a 1996 pretax profit target of T$1.03 billion on sales of T$31 billion.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
